IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOkuhfQ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-12T21:28:50Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T21:29:23Z","body":"> Vulkan also supports centroid interpolation.\n\nOpenGL also supports this, but not OpenGL ES or WebGL, so this can't be used on Compatibility without it breaking on some platforms.\n\nI don't know if Direct3D 12 and Metal support it either.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5273002365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5273424842","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122349#issuecomment-5273424842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122349","id":5273424842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOlITyg","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-12T22:17:57Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T22:17:57Z","body":"Centroid interpolation is supported in DX12 \n\nfrom https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct3d12/vrs\n\n<img width=\"969\" height=\"352\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/582861b3-ec41-400c-94c3-011739637c50\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5273424842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297960101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122349#issuecomment-5297960101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122349","id":5297960101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO8h0pQ","user":{"login":"Spekel","id":116194255,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuz7zw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116194255?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel","html_url":"https://github.com/Spekel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spekel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T20:39:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T20:39:52Z","body":"In my particular use case, I definitely get the best results by enabling per-sample interpolation:\n\n```glsl\n#ifdef NORMAL_USED\n#ifdef MODE_RENDER_NORMAL_ROUGHNESS\nlayout(location = 1) sample in vec3 normal_interp;\n#else\nlayout(location = 1) in vec3 normal_interp;\n#endif\n#endif\n```\n\nI would assume that this comes with additional cost, but the time for \"Render Depth Pre-Pass\" and \"Resolve Depth Pre-Pass (MSAA)\" remain constant for me when switching between centroid and sample interpolation. Maybe I'm not testing correctly. Centroid definitely prevents bad normals near curved surface edges, while sample noticably improves the visual quality of effects based on subpixel normals.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297960101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]